"app anatomy view" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		AppAnatomyView
		<header>Anatomy: the running app pulled apart into layers, in 3D, one for each view it draws.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>Anatomy shows how a running app is put together. Its switch is beside Inspect app in the top bar, or View › Anatomy (⌥⌘A). The app tilts back and comes apart into layers: the app at the bottom, each view it draws a layer above the view that holds it, each with a tag naming its type.</>
	<list class="spell-meta">
		<item icon="user">Written for: anyone changing the spell app's editor, or reading its code</>
		<item icon="image">A picture, not live: it needs the whole editor round it</>
	</>

	<section label="1. What it looks like">
		<icon slot="icon" name="image"/>
		<text paragraph>Solitaire, pulled apart in the app pane:</>
		<image src="/components/app/_images/AppAnatomyView.png" alt="Solitaire tilted back, its piles and cards lifted into layers, each tagged with its type" appearance="bordered rounded"/>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>A picture, taken by <text code>yarn site:pictures</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Using it">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Drag to turn it, scroll to zoom; Front looks straight at it again.</>
			<item>Spacing pulls the layers apart.</>
			<item>A click on a layer selects it, as a click on the app does: the Views tree, the properties and the code follow along. A double-click, or F, shows one layer and what's inside it alone; Esc goes back.</>
			<item>Views | Named | Outlines: Views shows the app itself on its layers, Named adds each layer's type as a tag, Outlines draws each layer as an empty frame. The full-window button lifts the pane over the editor.</>
			<item>The app keeps running: a card moved, or a live edit, shows on its layer. Hold ⌥ to play it.</>
			<item>Turned off, every style it set on the app is put back as it was. A view whose look cuts off what's inside it comes apart in one piece, its tag saying so.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Props, and where it's drawn">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-api family="AppAnatomyView"></>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>From its code, by <text code>yarn site:data</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

